{"id":"ENEE459B","title":"Topics in Computer Engineering; Computer Security and Reverse Engineering Laboratory","department":"Electrical & Computer Engineering","level":"Undergrad","credits":"3","description":"Minimum grade of C- in ENEE244, ENEE245, and ENEE350 or permission of the instructor.\n\nThis course focuses on software reverse engineering and low-level system analysis. Students will learn to analyze program execution, memory, and cryptography, using x86 assembly and reverse-engineering tools. The course also covers hardware attacks, fuzzing, symbolic execution, and defensive techniques, taught through lectures and hands-on labs. The goal is to build practical security analysis skills.","gradingMethods":null,"noLongerOffered":false,"removedTerm":null,"removedDetected":null,"terms":[{"term":"201808","sections":2,"seats":48,"openSeats":4,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gang Qu"],"removed":false},{"term":"201908","sections":2,"seats":48,"openSeats":7,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gang Qu"],"removed":false},{"term":"202008","sections":2,"seats":48,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gang Qu"],"removed":false},{"term":"202108","sections":2,"seats":48,"openSeats":2,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gang Qu"],"removed":false},{"term":"202208","sections":2,"seats":48,"openSeats":9,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Hassan Salmani"],"removed":false},{"term":"202308","sections":2,"seats":48,"openSeats":16,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Yonghwi Kwon","Hassan Salmani"],"removed":false},{"term":"202408","sections":2,"seats":48,"openSeats":20,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Yonghwi Kwon"],"removed":false},{"term":"202508","sections":2,"seats":45,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":3,"instructors":["Yonghwi Kwon"],"removed":false},{"term":"202601","sections":2,"seats":36,"openSeats":4,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Yonghwi Kwon"],"removed":false}],"instructors":[{"name":"Gang Qu","terms":4,"slug":"enee-gang-qu"},{"name":"Yonghwi Kwon","terms":4,"slug":"enee-yonghwi-kwon"},{"name":"Hassan Salmani",